on of foreign trade and policy that burden foreign products to encourage or safeguard domestic industry. Protective tariffs are among the most widely used instruments of protectionism, along with import quotas and export quotas and other non-tariff barriers to trade.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tariff","source":"Wikipedia","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"places":[{"title":"United States","extract":"The United States of America (USA), also known as the United States (U.S.) or America, is a country primarily located in North America. It is a federal republic consisting of 50 states and a federal capital district, Washington, D.C. The 48 contiguous states border Canada to the north and Mexico to the south, with the semi-exclave of Alaska in the northwest and the archipelago of Hawaii in the Pacific Ocean. The United States also asserts sovereignty over five major island territories and various uninhabited islands in Oceania and the Caribbean. It has the world's fourth-largest total area and third-largest population, exceeding 341 million.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States","source":"Wikipedia","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","iso2":"US"},{"title":"Mexico","extract":"Mexico, officially the United Mexican States, is a country in North America. It is the northernmost country in Latin America, bordering the United States of America to the north and Guatemala and Belize to the southeast, while having maritime boundaries with the Pacific Ocean to the west, the Caribbean Sea to the southeast, and the Gulf of Mexico to the east. Mexico covers 1,972,550 km2, and is the thirteenth-largest country in the world by land area. With a population around 131 million as of 2025, Mexico is the tenth-most populous country in the world and is home to the largest number of native Spanish speakers. Mexico City is the capital and largest city in Mexico, which ranks among the most populous metropolitan areas in the world.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mexico","source":"Wikipedia","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","iso2":"MX"}],"arc":{"reports":391,"first_seen":"2026-10-09T09:00:00Z","first_title":"Trump slashes tariffs to flood U.S. with 661 million pounds of foreign beef — Nebraska ranchers push back","first_url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMimgFBVV95cUxOTjJYSnRtdnlPT1pGWkVpN1ljTTF3emdfaWpfR1hXREJRRVRWU3VqSlpJZ0ZSZlhDYlUyUTFQeFQ1UmhvMEU4OFRGUEZtSi1LRWZaSENSWDFCeUNFR1dnckJPcXFmZW04bHNyWmNJdDNvd1pfZFF0bWhOZzFrWXhId19WTGZ2Q25FQWdVSGtOM2hRV1QxVVlOMy13?oc=5","first_publisher":"Yahoo Finance","earlier":[{"id":"e_f3be3a57f2fe","title":"Whitmer asks Trump administration to end food tariffs, reimburse Michiganders for increased costs","date":"2026-11-12T16:05:39Z","url":"https://news.google.?oc=5","publisher":"The Oakland Press","verification":"single_source_report"},{"id":"e_391e0d451bec","title":"Trump warns of new border ‘invasion’ after Dems’ midterm wins, threatens tariffs on Mexico","date":"2026-11-12T16:27:48Z","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMitwFBVV95cUxNUzdGc19ucnFZN2dXZ2FTeFk2aS1HYzZKS2Y2YXA1emExSFhrRXVPblJ2RU1GamYyYlFhd1ZZaHBGaFJvQkw4Zko0eWtqZGVkNWpiNmo2MldYVEZOQlhlSkMwZjZvOTBfSFZSUENJbjNEQkJkbjlvOVpJTjFoNHNGOFVUV1dxbmRxWUgyeXVwaXhZY0dRT3M3WnowZjlLNksxSUs5OTB0TVg1UFhSVlpHeEt3UEpQVjQ?oc=5","publisher":"Washington Times","verification":"single_source_report"},{"id":"e_4c1bd844ceb8","title":"Sheinbaum downplays migrant caravans as Trump threatens more tariffs","date":"2026-11-12T20:02:09Z","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMioAFBVV95cUxObWRIRmgtZkFPeHgxazlGbkRCZXJURGNmanc2ZGZMVHZzMkFndjltSVdMZHM1T1BNMGdGYTdIeFhtUFVJLU9ZcjBwcU03TjdXVWZnVm9FMnBzWG40U1laWFF2SFJaZG1rZmotbTh2WS0tenB0WXRtV1VLZU1fcURSdElaOVZjaHNkeGw5TzZVTkllbF95Ry1PUVVyZjVfMEx1?oc=5","publisher":"Courthouse News","verification":"single_source_report"},{"id":"e_bbf15ba531df","title":"Bipartisan push possible to curb Trump tariffs","date":"2026-11-12T20:06:50Z","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMimAFBVV95cUxONHZfWVlRVlczZnd4MnM2Qj